## The Development Process: AI-Assisted Iteration
### Real-Time Updates Without WebSockets
We used Streamlit’s _@st.fragment(run\_every=N)_ decorator that re-runs just the decorated function on a timer without reloading the full page.
@st.fragment(run_every=10)
def _live_section():
live = get_live_matches()
if live:
for i, match in enumerate(live):
_render_live_match(match, i)  
Combined with _@st.cache\_data(ttl=15)_ on API calls, this gives near-real-time updates with minimal ESPN API load. The live section refreshes every 10 seconds; schedule/results every 60 seconds; the banner every 60 seconds.
Flicker prevention: ESPN occasionally returns empty during brief CDN hiccups. This was prevented by buffering the last known state in _st.session\_state_:
if live:
st.session_state["_last_live"] = live
elif "_last_live" in st.session_state:
live = st.session_state["_last_live"]
